WEBVTT

NOTE Perfect Day (1929) - Riah TV captions

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
[music]

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.540
The bottle of coffee.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.980
I thought we'd
better take it along.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.540
Oh, that's fine. And now
where are they, Ollie?

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.360
They're in there.
And the potato chips?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.540
They're in, Ollie. Potato
chips, pickles, everything.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.970
Oh, that's fine. Aren't we
going to have a grand day?

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.340
Come on, Uncle. Need
your hat and coat.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.690
Come on.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.040
Janice, I'm not going to
leave this house today.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.650
Oh, but, Uncle, it's such a
perfectly gorgeous day for a

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.710
picnic.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.080
But this gout of
mine is killing me.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:57.010
I didn't sleep a
wink last night.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.000
Oh, but, Uncle, I think
you better come go with us.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.610
It'll be better in the sunshine.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.610
No, I've got a picnic
of my own right here.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.490
Now, listen, Uncle Ed,
you're going to go with us.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.840
Now, there's your cap and coat.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.540
You get them all. Hurry.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.960
Are the boys ready? They're
making the sandwiches.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.310
They'll be ready in a minute.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.350
We're

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.900
all ready.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.080
Isn't that wonderful?

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.030
Oh, there's still a
lot of sandwiches.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.660
Pick that up, Stanley.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.680
Throw that

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.120
back to me.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.530
You haven't any
right to push me.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.350
Well, you saw what
he did there, huh?

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.630
Please, you know what he wanted.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.980
Oh, boy, boy, boy, boy, boy.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.370
What was his fault?
Well, remember.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.930
Boy, boy.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.670
Remember, this is the Sabbath.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.020
It's

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:26.650
a day of peace.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.610
No more arguments from now on.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.050
No more arguments? That's right.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.640
Isn't it silly?
Yeah, sure it is.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.240
There it is, boys. Now let's
pick up the sandwiches.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.250
Oh, dear, I'll let
everything out.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:10.290
Oh!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.090
Now, give me

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:17.730
that tray. You pick up the
sandwiches, I'll hold the tray.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.650
I'm sorry, I couldn't help you.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.300
Oh, don't sorry me.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.440
Your pardon?

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:49.950
Well, I get a chance.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.040
No, you get the chance.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.510
And don't talk back.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.790
Come under that wheel.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:15.830
Look at me.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.050
Ollie,

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:41.490
I'll step on you in a minute.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.130
And don't call me Ollie.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.340
Shut up!

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:45.470
Why don't you do
something to help me?

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:47.920
What can I do?
